1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,959
Artinfact brings original PDFs, annotations, Markdown notes, whiteboards and a knowledge graph into one research
workspace. This tour introduces every

2
00:00:09,959 --> 00:00:21,910
major feature. Recorded scenes include the desktop plugin and a local preview of the same build. AI sections explain the
available workflows and controls.

3
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:32,203
Keep papers and notes together by research topic. Browse titles, authors and reading material in a shared workspace,
turning scattered files into a

4
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:34,888
research library you can keep building.

5
00:00:34,888 --> 00:00:46,044
Bring local PDFs, Markdown notes, images and editable whiteboard packages into one workspace. Keep original papers,
figures and your own records close at

6
00:00:46,044 --> 00:00:48,470
hand for reading and reuse.

7
00:00:48,470 --> 00:00:59,597
Miner U prepares Markdown, structured data, figures, tables, equations and source coordinates from a PDF. This is
automatic source preparation. The source

8
00:00:59,597 --> 00:01:10,725
used in this tour was parsed beforehand. The reader can open original PDF pages independently, while parsing and other
preparation happen separately.

9
00:01:10,725 --> 00:01:21,317
Browse and search full texts, sections, figures, equations, annotations and references. Choose the cards to bring onto your
board while retaining their

10
00:01:21,317 --> 00:01:23,242
connection to the source.

11
00:01:23,242 --> 00:01:33,804
Read original pages with the integrated Zotero PDF reader. Navigate, zoom, search and inspect the document structure,
with annotations and outlines

12
00:01:33,804 --> 00:01:37,324
alongside it and reading state stored locally.

13
00:01:37,324 --> 00:01:48,448
Capture highlights, underlines, notes and selected regions. Keep useful passages and figures together with your own
observations, ready to revisit or use

14
00:01:48,448 --> 00:01:50,976
as context for a question.

15
00:01:50,976 --> 00:02:01,038
AI Notes in the reader outline sidebar requests a section-by-section outline grounded in the paper. Each section can
include a short explanation to help

16
00:02:01,038 --> 00:02:11,518
you decide where to read next. The same outline entry is available in the source preparation menu. An outline updates
navigation rather than creating a

17
00:02:11,518 --> 00:02:12,357
whiteboard card.

18
00:02:12,357 --> 00:02:21,495
Request AI insights and annotations when you want help interpreting the paper. The agent reads the available source
material, develops insights with

19
00:02:21,495 --> 00:02:32,709
supporting evidence, and saves the result through MCP. Saved insights appear under the PDF in the plus library, ready for
you to choose and add to a

20
00:02:32,709 --> 00:02:35,617
board. This scene shows the entry points.

21
00:02:35,617 --> 00:02:46,672
Work on the material you choose: organize a card, summarize it, extract key points, translate it or give a custom research
instruction. Review proposed

22
00:02:46,672 --> 00:02:51,278
rewrites before accepting them where the editor offers that workflow.

23
00:02:51,278 --> 00:03:00,996
Table cards retain the original table image and its caption. The research menu can request an explanation of indicators,
results and comparison

24
00:03:00,996 --> 00:03:11,596
conditions. It also offers recognition as a Markdown table. The intended result keeps the editable explanation or table
above the original image, so you

25
00:03:11,596 --> 00:03:14,688
can compare the interpretation with its source.

26
00:03:14,688 --> 00:03:23,713
Formula cards render the original mathematical expression. Their research menu offers explanations of symbols,
step-by-step derivation, original

27
00:03:23,713 --> 00:03:34,861
definitions and applicable assumptions. You can also enter your own question. These are user-requested research actions,
with the source context available

28
00:03:34,861 --> 00:03:36,454
to the agent.

29
00:03:36,454 --> 00:03:46,727
Figure cards pair the original image with its caption and notes. Ask for the process, mechanism, figure description or
translation. When the host supports

30
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:56,144
it, an explanatory image can also be requested. You choose the instruction and send it when you want the agent to
participate.

31
00:03:56,144 --> 00:04:05,884
Use connections to express dependencies and background relationships. Give a comparison a clear scope by linking the
cards or papers whose methods and

32
00:04:05,884 --> 00:04:08,001
evidence you want to examine.

33
00:04:08,001 --> 00:04:18,694
Group related material around a common question. Request analysis of that region and keep resulting cards in the
research workspace, gradually building a

34
00:04:18,694 --> 00:04:20,553
source-backed line of argument.

35
00:04:20,553 --> 00:04:31,835
Create a board for each question. Arrange cards with dragging, resizing, colored regions and connections, using the same
material to develop different

36
00:04:31,835 --> 00:04:32,861
research views.

37
00:04:32,861 --> 00:04:43,522
Milkdown provides headings, lists, tasks, tables, code, mathematics and inline HTML. Notes also support highlighted text,
subscripts, superscripts and

38
00:04:43,522 --> 00:04:56,989
Mermaid diagrams. Select a card to edit. Table alignment controls appear beside the cell, and code blocks show their
language. Long content stays within

39
00:04:56,989 --> 00:05:00,356
the card and can be scrolled.

40
00:05:00,356 --> 00:05:11,340
Keep passages, paper identities and page references beside your analysis. Use the original PDF page to verify the context,
and distinguish what the source

41
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:13,628
says from what you infer.

42
00:05:13,628 --> 00:05:24,102
The knowledge graph is built from real Wiki pages and explicit links. Nodes represent sources, concepts, questions and
other knowledge. Drag a node to

43
00:05:24,102 --> 00:05:34,575
explore its neighborhood, then open its details to inspect related information or add it to a board. Graph settings control
layout spacing, soft or

44
00:05:34,575 --> 00:05:41,558
standard drag rebound, label visibility and font size. You can also zoom and change the theme.

45
00:05:41,558 --> 00:05:52,755
Link a note to an existing Pages page using its original link or page ID. With the Pages integration connected, you can
continue editing in the original

46
00:05:52,755 --> 00:06:02,294
page and synchronize its title and summary when requested. Local note text remains available. This scene shows the
association interface; it does not

47
00:06:02,294 --> 00:06:04,783
create or synchronize an external page.

48
00:06:04,783 --> 00:06:16,122
Export the board as a Markdown document with its image resources, or as an editable whiteboard package with a JSON
Canvas file. Regions become document

49
00:06:16,122 --> 00:06:27,007
sections, and connections help determine the order of cards. Folding does not shorten the exported text. Here, the
exported board contains nine cards, two

50
00:06:27,007 --> 00:06:30,182
connections, one region and three image resources.

51
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:40,599
Reference reading has two levels. Start with an abstract interpretation to understand what a cited paper is about. Choose
deeper reading when the full

52
00:06:40,599 --> 00:06:51,884
text is available. If needed, enable the option to download its PDF into the current workspace. You decide when to send
the request. An abstract summary

53
00:06:51,884 --> 00:06:55,357
and a full-paper reading have different evidence scopes.

54
00:06:55,357 --> 00:07:05,614
Reading templates provide a starting structure for the research question, method, evidence chain and limitations. Open
them from the plus library or the

55
00:07:05,614 --> 00:07:14,979
source preparation menu. Choose the structure you need, then develop your own observations and notes. Automatic
preparation supplies the material, while

56
00:07:14,979 --> 00:07:18,992
research instructions run when you choose to send them.

57
00:07:18,992 --> 00:07:30,792
Artinfact connects reading, evidence and your own notes. Start from the original source, choose where AI can help, and
take your work with you. Artinfact

58
00:07:30,792 --> 00:07:33,624
is free to use, by Hemistic.
